  "limits": [
    "A viewport smaller than a single owner minimum still needs a user-visible fallback. Chromium rejects that visible undersized request rather than silently applying clamped overlapping bounds.",
    "Native limits are learned from actual owner resizing, so the first constrained layout may briefly overshoot before reconciliation. Learned limits are not persisted.",
    "Physical keyboard/trackpad, physical drag, display transitions, fullscreen, popup geometry and large workloads remain unqualified. This run does not claim hardware delivery or input-ready latency.",
